      <Comment>In &lt;i&gt;Arabidopsis thaliana&lt;/i&gt;, a number of mutant alleles affected in the &lt;i&gt;MUR1&lt;/i&gt; gene were isolated which exhibited 50- to 200-fold reductions in L-fucose in the cell walls of shoot organs while the L-fucose content in roots was only reduced by 40% |CITS:[9050909]|. The &lt;i&gt;MUR1&lt;/i&gt; gene was expressed into &lt;i&gt;E.coli&lt;/i&gt; and shown to have GDP-D-mannose 4,6-dehydratase activity |CITS:[9050909]|. The enzyme was later purified and crystallized, demonstrating that it forms a tetramer complexed with NADPH and a GDP-sugar ligand. The same study crystallized a dimer complex but did not determine any catalytic acitvity for the dimer |CITS:[12501186]|. Another study showed that MUR1 alone, heterologously expressed in yeast cytoplasm, is unstable and requires interaction with |FRAME:AT1G73250-MONOMER| (GER1) |CITS:[12881408]|.</Comment>
